-- title:
--   Places above j=j₀ count moduli points with that j-invariant
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number and let $j_0$ lie in the algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}$. Assume [`ModularCurve.EMD N j₀`](def/ModularCurve_EMD.html#L46): there is a Weierstrass curve $E_0$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ which is elliptic, with $j(E_0)=j_0$, together with a bijection $\Phi$ from [`ModularCurve.Emb N j₀`](def/ModularCurve_EMD.html#L22) onto [`ModularCurve.CycSub E₀ N`](def/ModularCurve_EMD.html#L36) — the subgroups of $E_0(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ of the form $\mathbb{Z}g$ for a point $g$ of additive order exactly $N$ — such that two members $\psi,\psi'$ of `Emb N j₀` satisfy `SamePlace`, i.e. there is a single place $w$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}F_N$ with `Induces ψ w` and `Induces ψ' w`, precisely when $\Phi\psi$ and $\Phi\psi'$ satisfy `SameOrbit`, i.e. are generated by points $g,g'$ with $g'$ the image of $g$ under the inverse of a Weierstrass variable change fixing $E_0$. Here $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}F_N$ is `modularFunctionFieldBar N`, the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((t))$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ by the coefficientwise images of the field of modular functions of level $N$ (itself generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the divisor expansions), and a place is a proper valuation subring containing $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ which is a principal ideal ring, with $\mathrm{ord}$ the associated normalised integer valuation. Let $S$ be a finite set of places of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}F_N$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ consisting exactly of those $v$ with $\mathrm{ord}_v(\bar\jmath_N - j_0)>0$, where $\bar\jmath_N$ is the coefficient-extended $q$-expansion of the modular invariant. Then the cardinality of $S$ equals the number of elements $x$ of `ModuliPoint N (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` — the quotient of the pairs (elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, point of order $N$) by the relation generated by variable changes combined with multiplication of the marked point by an integer coprime to $N$ — with $j(x)=j_0$.
--
--   This identifies the points of $X_0(N)$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying above a given value $j_0$ of the modular invariant with the isomorphism classes of pairs (elliptic curve, cyclic subgroup of order $N$) having that $j$-invariant, conditionally on the embedding–moduli dictionary at $j_0$. It is used in the computation of the numbers of elliptic points $\nu_2,\nu_3$ of $X_0(N)$, via the fibres above $j=1728$ and $j=0$, and in the construction of divisors for the Riemann–Roch estimates on $X_0(N)$.
